cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CIV.IQ"
message: "If you use CIV.IQ in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Sandford
    given-names: Mark
    email: contact@civdotiq.org
repository-code: "https://github.com/civdotiq/civ.iq"
url: "https://civdotiq.org"
abstract: >-
  Nonpartisan civic intelligence platform connecting 19 government data
  sources to provide transparent access to congressional voting records,
  campaign finance, lobbying disclosures, federal spending, and
  legislative analysis. Includes 12 statistical analyzers, ML-based
  vote prediction, and entity resolution across government databases.
keywords:
  - civic technology
  - government transparency
  - campaign finance
  - congressional voting
  - lobbying
  - open data
  - civic intelligence
license: MIT
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2025-09-02"
